599	    /** One neighbor's impedance + permeation, sampled from a single {@code descriptor}/{@code
600	     *  material} read each so both values come from the same baked generation — reading them via
601	     *  two separate accessor calls let a concurrent rebake land in between, mixing an old
602	     *  impedance with a new permeation (or vice versa) for the same neighbor. */
603	    private record NeighborSample(double impedance, double permeation) {
604	        static final NeighborSample MISSING = new NeighborSample(Double.NaN, Double.NaN);
605	    }
